/* catchup1 PLY4: the minigame state constants main's ov006 TUs read as TYPED
 * pointers to member (260 rows over bomroom, pachinko, pachinko2, curling,
 * curling2, sound, teresa, slots, heyho_obj_adapter and unit020b4aa4). Same
 * rule as above, keyed on the config symbol's address (ovNNN symbols.txt)
 * because these names carry no address for pmfvalues.py to parse; the list is
 * every UNDEF pmf_* the compiled TUs ask for (dumpbin), census in the run's
 * lane PLY4's report. Three shapes:
 *   member  {&member, 0} straight;
 *   drop1   the ROM state function takes no argument while its table passes
 *           one: a __fastcall thunk of the table's arity pops it;
 *   flat    a free function taking the receiver first: a __fastcall thunk
 *           forwards (this[, arg]) to the cdecl body.
 * Raw records (pmf_* the TUs declare as structs, ints or words and copy as
 * data) are not here: they stay ROM bytes and keep the DS-address route. A
 * C-linkage name only takes this value once port/ov006_syms.txt stops
 * mounting the same name from ROM bytes.
 */

